-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      NexClash differential verification against four recordings;
              simulated boot; the interrupt fix checked to leave the handlers'
              state unchanged; run from its menu in OverSpec; Tang FPGA board:
              loads and plays. 1.0 played by the owner on a ZX Spectrum Next
              (KS3), 2026-11-26: plays. Played by the owner on a ZX Spectrum
              Next (KS3), 2026-11-27: the player and the Enhanced colours look
              good; the scroll steps 8 pixels at a time, as the original; at
              game over the game stops on its GAME OVER screen, waiting for
              its tape. 1.2 (player two and the enemies painted) played by the
              owner in OverSpec, 2026-11-27: good. 1.3 (Smooth scroll, game
              over to the title) played by the owner in OverSpec, 2026-11-28:
              good.

  Replay      Four recordings per sprite edition (32,291 frames). OverSpec
              checked 26,005 updates across all five builds. Both smooth
              builds met every beat. JNext matched all ten fresh and restarted
              states. (NexClash record altered_beast, verified 2026-11-28;
              this build is byte-identical to it)

  Emulator    1.3, 2026-11-28: OverSpec checked 26,005 updates across all five
              builds against the original's state; with Smooth scroll, 150 and
              250 consecutive frames with no pixel blinking off for a frame;
              2-pixel steps keep the checkerboard textures still (1-pixel
              steps changed 25% of the playfield at each step); JNext played
              every build to game over and a second game, each matching a
              fresh start.

  Hardware    ZX Spectrum Next (Kickstarter 3), System/Next 26.11a: 1.1 played
              by the owner, the player and the Enhanced colours look good; the
              scroll steps 8 pixels at a time, as the original; at game over
              the game stops on its GAME OVER screen, waiting for its tape;
              1.2 and 1.3 not yet run on hardware (earlier: Tang Nano 20K FPGA
              build of the Next: loads with DivMMC automap on and plays;
              without the interrupt fix it crashed within 8 seconds)

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
